# Take the wash count off the products whose size is a printed sum or short word
# (backend backlog plan 0029, built as plan 0279).
# post.sh runs `node wash-sizes.js --selection sum-and-short-word` inside the
# harvester pod. It selects every ACTIVE bound row whose printed size is a sum
# of washes (`35+18 lavados`, `30+6lav`) or El Jamón's short word (`40lav`,
# `60lv`), and every product of such a row that is UNIT and holds that count as
# its size. Each product then loses its size through an ordinary item update
# with the harvester's actor: one catalog transaction per product. The pack
# count stays. No price changes, nothing is deleted, no size is set. The
# selection is disjoint from task 0007's, so the two run in either order.
#
# The products it corrects are listed for the curator in the ConfigMap
# release-task-0009-review of the namespace (plan 0279, section 5), and the
# rows it notes and does not correct beside them. Neither script prints a
# line of either list.
#
# The deploy unit whose release runs this task (k8s plan 0015 D9).
UNIT="velista"
RUN_UNTIL_STAGING="2026-12-03"
RUN_UNTIL_PRODUCTION="2026-12-10"
# The velista release that carries this task, after tasks 0007 and 0008
# (owner decision O3 of plan 0279, 2026-11-26).
PRODUCTION_RELEASE="0.20.0"
# The task writes only catalog. The harvester database is read.
DATABASES="catalog"
#
# The most products the task may change. check.sh counts them with `--count`
# and refuses above this number, and post.sh counts again and passes it to the
# command as `--max`, which refuses too. An empty value is not a number, so
# both scripts refuse it.
#
# Measured read only on 2026-11-26 on a restored copy of the staging data of
# 2026-11-20 (itself a copy of production of 2026-11-19): 74 products (12
# DEZA, 62 El Jamón). 80 is that count rounded up to the next ten, for each.
# No pod of either cluster was counted for this commit. Write other numbers
# only after reading the count that the check phase prints, never to get past
# it.
MAX_PRODUCTS_STAGING="80"
MAX_PRODUCTS_PRODUCTION="80"
